  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> and <math><mi>g</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be respectively given by <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Define <math><mi>h</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> by <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Then number of points at which <math><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not differentiable is_________",
